Z||000001||Philphine||10-21-2001||11:27 PM||||i've got some 17x10 with 275/40-17s on them, but i still havent done the 6000 swap to know how/if they'll fit. i have 17x8.5 for the front but i'm thinking around 235 or 245/40-17. the overall diameter is closer to stock. seems like that would be needed for turning and clearance more so than in the rear. but since i haven't done it all this is guesswork.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Formula88||10-21-2001||11:45 PM||||Keep in mind, wider tires and manual steering = Popeye forearms.  Personally, I would think 235 or 245 as the absolute comfortable limit for driving.  But that's me.  As for tires, I'd recommend Pirelli P7000 Supersports, Bridgestone RE730, or Bridgestone PolePosition S-03.  The S-03 is probably the best.  I'll probably go with RE730s on my car when I get my 17s.||||reg||1
